// InfoVC
"InfoVC.Title" = "Matrix 3x3";

"InfoVC.LabelMatrix3x3.Description" = "In mathematics, a matrix is a rectangular array or table of numbers, symbols, or expressions, arranged in rows and columns, which is used to represent a mathematical object or a property of such an object. Matrix 3x3 has 3 columns and 3 rows";

"InfoVC.LabelMainDiagonal.Info" = "To find the determinant(D) of the 3x3 matrix, you need to add three products of elements standing on the main diagonal(Red Colour) and at the vertices of isosceles triangles with a side parallel to this diagonal.\n\nMain Diagonal = (a11a22a33) + (a12a23a31) + (a13a21a32)";

"InfoVC.LabelSecondaryDiagonal.Info" = "Then you need to subtract three products of elements standing on the secondary diagonal(Red Colour) and at the vertices of isosceles triangles with a side parallel to this diagonal\n\nSecondary Diagonal = (a13a22a31) - (a12a21a33) - (a11a23a32)";

"InfoVC.LabelDeterminant.Info" = "The Determinant will be:\nD = Main Diagonal - Secondary Diagonal";

// InstructionVC
"InstructionVC.Title" = "Instruction";

"InstructionVC.Page1.Text" = "Two players need to choose the sign: (+) or (-). The first move is made by the player (+) with a blue color 🔵 and then the player (-) with a red color 🔴 .\n\n2. The game field is a Matrix 3х3, which consists of the 9 cells. You should enter the number inside the each cell from 1 to 9.\n\n3. Since all the cells have been filled you will see the Determinant value - D and a winner.\n\nFor restart press Start Over. Info section will provide you information about the Matrix 3x3. Note: To activate the numpad you should tap any cell first.";

"InstructionVC.Page2.Text" = "Enjoy the Game!";

